<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>DTP homepage concept — Board Briefing</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    :root{--paper:#efeee8;--ink:#101115;--muted:#5f6570;--soft:#d9d7cf;--dark:#050507;--navy:#171a2c;--mint:#05cc90;--rule:rgba(16,17,21,.16)}
    *{box-sizing:border-box} body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:'IBM Plex Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1.45} a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.mono{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace}.wrap{max-width:1160px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px}.top{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);background:rgba(239,238,232,.9);backdrop-filter:blur(14px);position:sticky;top:0;z-index:4}.nav{height:74px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center}.brand{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-weight:700;font-size:18px}.navlinks{display:flex;gap:26px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}.cta-small{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);padding:10px 14px;border-radius:999px}.hero{padding:86px 0 54px}.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:54px;align-items:end}.eyebrow{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';font-size:13px;color:#0b8c66;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.hero h1{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:clamp(54px,7.2vw,94px);letter-spacing:-.065em;line-height:.98;margin:18px 0 22px}.hero .lead{font-size:22px;color:#3e4450;max-width:650px;margin:0 0 32px}.button-row{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;border:1px solid var(--ink);padding:15px 18px;border-radius:999px;font-weight:600}.btn.primary{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}.btn.secondary{background:transparent}.brief{border:1px solid var(--rule);background:#f8f7f2;padding:28px;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:12px 12px 0 #d8d7ce}.brief-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);padding-bottom:16px;margin-bottom:18px}.brief-title{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-weight:700;font-size:24px}.brief-kv{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:12px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.brief-kv span:first-child{color:var(--muted)}.brief-note{margin-top:18px;background:rgba(5,204,144,.12);border-left:4px solid var(--mint);padding:16px;color:#23342f}.band{background:var(--dark);color:var(--paper);margin-top:44px;padding:70px 0}.band-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.12);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12)}.band-card{background:var(--dark);padding:28px;min-height:230px}.band-card span{color:var(--mint)}.band-card h3{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:28px;margin:42px 0 12px}.band-card p{color:#b9bfca;margin:0}.section{padding:78px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.section-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:54px}.section h2{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:clamp(38px,4.6vw,62px);line-height:.98;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:10px 0 16px}.section p.large{font-size:20px;color:#3f4652}.list{display:grid;gap:14px}.item{display:grid;grid-template-columns:76px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.item b{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';color:#0b8c66}.item h3{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:25px;margin:0 0 6px}.item p{color:var(--muted);margin:0}.proof{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px;margin-top:28px}.proof-card{background:#fffef9;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;padding:22px}.proof-card h3{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:24px;margin:0 0 10px}.proof-card p{color:var(--muted);margin:0}.final{background:var(--navy);color:var(--paper);padding:76px 0}.final-inner{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}.final h2{font-family:'Space Grotesk';font-size:52px;line-height:1;margin:0 0 16px}.final p{color:#c6cad5;font-size:19px}.final .btn{border-color:var(--mint);background:var(--mint);color:#02130d}@media(max-width:900px){.hero-grid,.section-grid,.final-inner,.proof{grid-template-columns:1fr}.band-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.navlinks{display:none}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="top"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Digital Technology Partner</a><div class="navlinks"><a href="#problem">Problem</a><a href="#route">Route</a><a href="#proof">Proof</a><a class="cta-small" href="#start">Start</a></div></div></header>
  <main>
    <section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">// Leadership briefing, not AI theatre</div><h1>Most AI projects start in the wrong place.</h1><p class="lead">Before you build another tool, leadership needs to know what people are already doing, where the risk sits, which opportunities are real, and what the organisation is actually ready to absorb.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="btn primary" href="#start">Book a readiness discussion</a><a class="btn secondary" href="#route">Read the route</a></div></div><aside class="brief"><div class="brief-head"><div><div class="mono">DTP / board note</div><div class="brief-title">AI Adoption Readiness</div></div><div class="eyebrow">Draft</div></div><div class="brief-kv"><span>Current state</span><strong>Experimentation without visibility</strong></div><div class="brief-kv"><span>Leadership risk</span><strong>Decisions based on anecdotes</strong></div><div class="brief-kv"><span>Useful output</span><strong>Evidence-led next steps</strong></div><div class="brief-note">The question is not “can we build AI?”. The question is “what should we encourage, control, investigate, stop or prove next?”.</div></aside></div></section>
    <section class="band" id="problem"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">// Why this matters now</div><div class="band-grid"><article class="band-card"><span class="mono">01</span><h3>Experimentation is already happening.</h3><p>Teams are using AI in pockets, often faster than policies, training or operating models can keep up.</p></article><article class="band-card"><span class="mono">02</span><h3>Leadership sees fragments.</h3><p>A demo here, a risk there, a promising idea somewhere else. Not enough to make a coherent decision.</p></article><article class="band-card"><span class="mono">03</span><h3>Build decisions get premature.</h3><p>Without readiness evidence, companies either overbuild, underinvest, or chase the loudest use case.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="route"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">// The DTP route</div><h2>Start with decision quality.</h2><p class="large">We help you understand the adoption landscape first, then move into proof of concept, MVP or pilot work only where there is enough evidence to justify it.</p></div><div class="list"><div class="item"><b>01</b><div><h3>Readiness Snapshot</h3><p>A low-friction entry point for directional signal and qualification.</p></div></div><div class="item"><b>02</b><div><h3>Readiness Diagnostic</h3><p>An evidence base leadership can trust before deciding what to encourage, control, investigate or stop.</p></div></div><div class="item"><b>03</b><div><h3>Readiness Advisory</h3><p>Interpretation, challenge and leadership playback, not another dashboard dumped in your lap.</p></div></div><div class="item"><b>04</b><div><h3>Proof, MVP, pilot</h3><p>Where the case is strong, we build the focused thing that proves value in the real operating environment.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="proof"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">// DTP still delivers systems</div><h2>Understanding first. Building second. Operating value throughout.</h2><div class="proof"><article class="proof-card"><h3>AI and automation delivery</h3><p>Agents, workflow tools, data pipelines, reporting systems, internal apps and proof-of-concept builds.</p></article><article class="proof-card"><h3>Leadership and operating model support</h3><p>Decision packs, adoption maps, governance boundaries, prioritised opportunities and implementation routes.</p></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="final" id="start"><div class="wrap final-inner"><div><div class="eyebrow">// Next sensible step</div><h2>Find out what AI should mean inside your organisation.</h2><p>Not in general. Not in a vendor slide deck. In your teams, your constraints, your risks and your operating reality.</p></div><a class="btn" href="https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/f0762b9af6a94ed2add9818a4f3ca4e5@digitaltechnologypartner.ai/meetingtype/qc2lOXjEdkO6GkMS_jZJrQ2?anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a discovery call</a></div></section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
